				"description": "Thrown by run when a non-empty line of the CLI's stdout is not JSON. It is raised before the result is read, so it carries no usage or reportedModel."
			},
			{
				"name": "TaskOutputOverflowError",
				"type": "thrown",
				"description": "Rejected with the message 'Task CLI output exceeded its bound.' when the CLI's stdout passes 8,000,000 characters; the process group is killed first."
			},
			{
				"name": "AbortSignal.reason",
				"type": "propagated",
				"description": "input.signal's reason (a DOMException named AbortError unless abort() was given another reason) when the signal is aborted before the CLI starts or while it runs; an abort kills the CLI's process group first."
			},
			{
				"name": "NodeJS.ErrnoException",
				"type": "propagated",
				"description": "The spawn error when the CLI cannot be started, for example ENOENT when claude or codex is not on PATH."
			},
			{
				"name": "resourceWork rejection",
				"type": "propagated",
				"description": "Rejections from resourceWork while it reserves the 2048 MiB coding slot pass through, for example 'Resource queue is full', a wait timeout, 'Resource request exceeds usable capacity after reserves', or a SyntaxError from an invalid queue config.json."
			}
		],
